Fishburble is the bubbling, gurgling language of fishmen and other aquatic
humanoids. It is designed to be spoken underwater, where its burbling tones
and popping sounds carry clearly through the depths.

Surface dwellers find Fishburble extremely difficult to learn, as many of
its sounds require water to form properly. Speakers above the waves must
approximate these sounds as best they can, often sounding comical to native
speakers.

Knowledge of Fishburble proves invaluable when exploring coastal waters,
underwater ruins, or dealing with the mysterious fishfolk who sometimes
emerge to trade with surface settlements. These secretive beings guard many
secrets of the deep.

